From 7a1d132ec0131b36f40e5c66dc157f77e7005abc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:18:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] koblitz_index_calculus: the collection scan pipelined
 across trials

A walked collection run now prepares trial t's rests and keys before it
reads trial t-1's presence filter.  While trial t's keys are formed,
sixteen at a time, trial t-1's filter words are prefetched into the
second-level cache in proportion, so the probe pass finds them there
instead of waiting on the last-level cache or memory one round trip at a
time.  Each trial's answer depends only on its own point and scan, and
trials are pushed in order, so the run's output is the one-call scan's;
a test checks the first witness trial for trial, for a wrapping window
and an index list, and that the paced keys equal the bulk keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013vyAr6TGoMhy56CQmvaUCd
