From 0472164f73e422c63fbc19f621d55113e2446ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:55:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] koblitz_index_calculus: the pipelined scan in three
 stages

A run's walked probes are formed first and then scanned by
`scan_pipelined`: trial i is prepared while trial i-1's filter words come
in, trial i-1 is filtered and its admitted keys' bucket entries sent for,
and trial i-2 is resolved after its runs were sent for before trial i was
prepared.  Each key's filter hash is computed once and kept.  The answers
come back in trial order and are the one-call scan's; a test checks them
with trials that do not scan and scans the stages refuse mixed in, for runs
of every length from none to past the pipeline's depth.

`examples/pipe_scan_bench` times the one-call scan against the split forms
on a real folded table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013vyAr6TGoMhy56CQmvaUCd
---
