From 923210ffdbb007fc024cba8bd2a5eafddb43a538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:55:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] koblitz_fast: the key's rotation step in fewer micro-ops

`v << 1` becomes `v + v`, which issues on either vector port where a shift
has one, and `v >> (n - 1)` a per-lane variable shift, one micro-op where
a shift by a count in a vector register is two on Skylake-SP and Cascade
Lake.  The same value lane for lane; the laned-key tests pass unchanged.
The paced keys pause twice per group, before and after the rotation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013vyAr6TGoMhy56CQmvaUCd
---
